{"check_id":"IAC-K8S-RUN_AS_ROOT-01","module":"iac","title":"Container has no explicit non-root execution guard","severity":"medium","base_severity":"medium","confidence":"medium","cwe":"CWE-269","owasp":"A02:2025","cvss":{"vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N","score":5.4},"location":{"path":"bench/corpora/_slices/k8s-scenarios/root/kubernetes-goat-home/deployment.yaml","match_digest":"dc64336a2d181fbc","occurrence":"0","line":15},"logical":{"kind":"file","fqn":"bench/corpora/_slices/k8s-scenarios/root/kubernetes-goat-home/deployment.yaml:15"},"evidence":"      containers","remediation":"Set securityContext.runAsNonRoot to true (and pair it with a non-zero\nrunAsUser) at the pod or container level. Without it, the container image's own\ndefault user applies, which for most public base images is root - a container\nbreakout then lands the attacker in the host's root context rather than an\nunprivileged one.","references":["CWE-269"],"cis":[],"exposure":"unknown","auth":"user","sensitive_data":false,"cell":"bench/corpora/_slices/k8s-scenarios/root","status":"new","first_seen":"2026-09-10T11:22:14Z","last_seen":"2026-09-10T11:22:14Z","suppressed":false,"suppressed_by":null,"contributors":[],"derived_into":[],"related":[],"endpoint_hosts":[],"rule_digest":"19ead7b4e73d350c0cae6b71ed8babe502273b9c5f4e96bcd0b9b21d77ca8cb2","fingerprint":"9cac1d4269880212745a876dce1fb814fdee512c83f38674ad47df3a80bcaa9a"}
{"check_id":"IAC-K8S-SA_TOKEN_DEFAULT-01","module":"iac","title":"Pod does not disable automatic service-account token mounting","severity":"medium","base_severity":"medium","confidence":"medium","cwe":"CWE-269","owasp":"A01:2025","cvss":{"vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N","score":5.4},"location":{"path":"bench/corpora/_slices/k8s-scenarios/root/kubernetes-goat-home/deployment.yaml","match_digest":"ca440b5701c641ed","occurrence":"0","line":2},"logical":{"kind":"file","fqn":"bench/corpora/_slices/k8s-scenarios/root/kubernetes-goat-home/deployment.yaml:2"},"evidence":"kind: Deployment","remediation":"Set automountServiceAccountToken to false on the pod spec (or the\nServiceAccount) unless the workload genuinely calls the Kubernetes API. The default is\ntrue, so every pod otherwise carries a live, mountable credential for its service\naccount into a container that most workloads never use it from - exactly what a\ncontainer-escape or SSRF exploit looks for next.","references":["CWE-269"],"cis":[],"exposure":"unknown","auth":"user","sensitive_data":false,"cell":"bench/corpora/_slices/k8s-scenarios/root","status":"new","first_seen":"2026-09-10T11:22:14Z","last_seen":"2026-09-10T11:22:14Z","suppressed":false,"suppressed_by":null,"contributors":[],"derived_into":[],"related":[],"endpoint_hosts":[],"rule_digest":"972f26b12228894e2601b2f1ff564f37e5dd89072f92c0dc8f9df93988223820","fingerprint":"d90b4b5603f5a017cab6f4b985d4d28342be8dc83e0d086947e969576b99df60"}
