{"check_id":"IAC-K8S-PRIVILEGED-01","module":"iac","title":"Container runs with privileged escalation enabled","severity":"critical","base_severity":"critical","confidence":"high","cwe":"CWE-269","owasp":"A02:2025","cvss":{"vector":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:L/A:N","score":5.4},"location":{"path":"bench/corpora/_slices/k8s-scenarios/root/system-monitor/deployment.yaml","match_digest":"9f26cf058af1fb19","occurrence":"0","line":41},"logical":{"kind":"file","fqn":"bench/corpora/_slices/k8s-scenarios/root/system-monitor/deployment.yaml:41"},"evidence":"          privileged: true","remediation":"Remove `privileged: true` from the container's securityContext.\nA privileged container has near-complete access to the host - device nodes, kernel\ncapabilities, and namespaces - so almost every real workload can run instead with a\nnarrow, explicit `capabilities.add` list for only the capability it actually needs.","references":["CWE-269"],"cis":[],"exposure":"unknown","auth":"user","sensitive_data":false,"cell":"bench/corpora/_slices/k8s-scenarios/root","status":"new","first_seen":"2026-09-10T11:22:14Z","last_seen":"2026-09-10T11:22:14Z","suppressed":false,"suppressed_by":null,"contributors":[],"derived_into":[],"related":[],"endpoint_hosts":[],"rule_digest":"4ddd873dfef3d2338036f4bb273884a0eaab9ee26821ee6124be41e68fd92744","fingerprint":"fd7f836ce8c2f5c127afb8ed187deb00f2cc3fb8db0a49e4f10730a09dac5d8b"}
